<title>USA: Raychem Corp Q2 shr $1.14 vs $0.55.</title>
<headline>Raychem Corp Q2 shr $1.14 vs $0.55.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dec. 31, 1996     Q2     Dec. 31, 1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.14		    $0.55</p>
<p> Net			 52,435		   25,102</p>
<p> Revs		    441,047		   411,051</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	46,119		   45,856</p>
<p>					 6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.71		    $1.27</p>
<p> Net			125,155		   57,532</p>
<p> Revs		     871,358		  821,566</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  46,106		   45,381</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Latest second quarter income includes &quot;approximately&quot; $6 million in pretax severance and plant consolidation costs. Year-ago second quarter income includes a $19 million pretax share of Raynet operating losses and a net $5 million one-time pretax charge. Excluding those items, pretax income rose to $68 million in the second quarter, from $59 million in the year ago period, the company said.</p>
